  "body": "## Summary\n- Moves `actions.tf`, `claude-ops.tf`, `github-ops.tf` from the root into `repos/`\n- Wraps them in a `repos` child module (`repos.tf` at root), called with the `github` provider explicitly passed through\n- Adds `repos/versions.tf` (`required_providers`, needed for that explicit pass-through — same fix already applied to `modules/github-repo`) and `repos/outputs.tf` (re-exports the `repos` map)\n- Root `outputs.tf` now reads `module.repos.repos` instead of referencing the three repo modules directly\n\n## Verification\nRan `terraform init -backend=false` locally: it correctly resolved the full nested module graph (`repos.actions`/`repos.claude-ops`/`repos.github-ops`, each under `modules/github-repo`) before failing only on the provider *download* itself — this sandbox has no network access to the Terraform registry, unrelated to the config.",
